# How S-BOM Scans Projects & Finds Vulnerabilities

> A complete walkthrough of how your code goes from a folder on disk to a list of CVEs with risk scores.

---

## The Big Picture (30-Second Summary)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["📁 Your Project Folder"] --> B["🔍 Find Manifest Files"]
    B --> C["📋 Extract Package List"]
    C --> D["🌐 Ask OSV: Any known bugs?"]
    D --> E["🏛️ Ask MITRE/NVD: How bad is it?"]
    E --> F["⚠️ CVE List + Risk Score"]
```

**In plain English:** The scanner looks at your project folder, finds files like `package.json` or `requirements.txt`, reads the list of libraries you use, then checks online databases to see if any of those libraries have known security bugs (CVEs). For each bug found, it fetches a severity score (CVSS) and tells you how dangerous it is.

---

## Phase 1: How Does the Scan Start?

There are **three ways** a scan can begin:

| Trigger | What Happens | Code |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Local Upload** | User uploads a zip, folder, or single manifest file from the UI | [server.py `/api/v1/scans/local`](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/api/server.py#L134-L229) |
| **GitHub Repository** | User pastes a GitHub URL; the backend clones the repo | [server.py `/api/v1/scans/github`](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/api/server.py#L231-L285) |
| **GitHub Webhook** | A `push` or `release` event auto-triggers a scan | [server.py `/api/v1/github/webhooks`](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/api/server.py#L652-L710) |

In all three cases, the request ends up at [Orchestrator.create_scan()](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/scans/orchestrator.py#L63-L120) which:

1. Creates a **scan record** in the database (status = `PENDING`)
2. Puts a **job** into a queue
3. A background **worker** picks up the job and calls [Orchestrator.execute()](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/scans/orchestrator.py#L166-L251)

Think of it like ordering food at a restaurant — you place the order (create scan), it goes to the kitchen queue (job queue), and a chef picks it up (worker executes).

