## Phase 5: Enrichment & Compliance

Still in [pipeline.py](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/scanner/pipeline.py):

### Local Enrichment ([enrich_local()](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/scanner/pipeline.py#L217-L252))

The scanner does extra work to fill in gaps:

1. **License Detection**: If a package doesn't declare its license, the scanner looks for `LICENSE`, `LICENSE.md`, `COPYING`, or `NOTICE` files in the package directory and reads them to identify `MIT`, `Apache-2.0`, `GPL-3.0`, or `BSD-3-Clause`.

2. **PURL Generation**: If a package doesn't have a Package URL, one is constructed: `pkg:{ecosystem}/{name}@{version}`

3. **Hash Collection**: Integrity hashes (`SHA-256`, `SHA-512`, `SHA-1`, `MD5`) are collected from lockfiles for supply-chain verification.

### NTIA Compliance Audit ([audit_compliance()](file:///d:/Work_Stuff/Projects/S-BOM/backend/app/scanner/pipeline.py#L255-L273))

Every component is checked against the **NTIA Minimum Elements** for a valid SBOM:

| Check | What It Means | Pass if... |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `ntia_supplier` | Who made this package? | Has a supplier name (not `NOASSERTION`) |
| `ntia_name` | What is it called? | Has a name |
| `ntia_version` | What version? | Has a version |
| `ntia_identifier` | Unique ID? | Has a PURL or CPE |
| `ntia_relationship` | How is it connected? | Is marked direct or appears in dependency graph |
| `ntia_author` | Who created the SBOM? | Scanner name is present |
| `ntia_timestamp` | When was it generated? | Timestamp is present |

A component **passes compliance** only if ALL seven checks are true.

